rowhammer (0.22.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New play screen layout: the fixed 48x24 block is now centered in the
    terminal instead of hugging the top left corner. The hold piece and
    a key legend sit in the left pane, the board in the middle, the
    three upcoming pieces in the top right pane, and the round counters
    (name, lines, rows, level, gold/silver, play time, wonder progress)
    on the two bottom status lines. Pause and game over are drawn as a
    box over the board, the latter carrying the highscore rank.
  * Rendering is incremental: draw_frame assembles the screen into
    FRAME_LINES and render_flush writes only the lines that actually
    changed, each with its own cursor positioning. Settled board rows
    are cached and rebuilt only after the board really changed, so a
    moving piece costs a handful of rows instead of all 200 cells.
    Measured against the previous full-frame renderer: about half the
    time per frame and roughly a fourteenth of the terminal output.
  * Leaving the game while a round is still suspended in the pause menu
    now asks for confirmation ("Wirklich beenden?", declining option
    preselected) instead of silently ending and recording that round.
  * Autowrap is turned off while the alternate screen is active: at the
    48x24 minimum the layout fills the very last terminal cell, which
    could otherwise scroll the screen on some terminals.

 -- roemer2201 <r.oliver@web.de>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200

rowhammer (0.21.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add configurable colors via named color themes. A theme maps every
    piece type and the gold/silver squares to symbolic color names, each
    carrying a basic (8/16-color ANSI) and an extended (xterm 256-color)
    meaning. Four themes ship: "guideline" (the previous default look,
    unchanged), "classic", "mono" and "colorblind" (deuteranopia-friendly).
    Selectable in the settings menu (with a live per-theme color swatch),
    via --color-theme NAME and the ROWHAMMER_COLOR_THEME environment
    variable, and persisted to the user config file (COLOR_THEME).

 -- roemer2201 <r.oliver@web.de>  Sat, 26 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200

rowhammer (0.20.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cleared rows now blink before they vanish: when a lock completes one
    or more rows, those rows flash twice (highlighted / normal, about
    280 ms in total) and only then are removed and the next piece
    spawns. The rows are collected before the clear (board_full_rows),
    the renderer highlights them via FLASH_ROWS/FLASH_STATE and
    flash_rows drives the animation; duration and cycle count are
    adjustable via FLASH_MS/FLASH_CYCLES (FLASH_CYCLES=0 disables it).
    Square detection still runs first, so a row through a freshly built
    gold/silver square flashes at its full value.

 -- roemer2201 <r.oliver@web.de>  Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200

rowhammer (0.19.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Handle terminal resizing while the game runs (SIGWINCH). The fixed
    board+sidebar layout still needs at least 48x24, but a resize is now
    caught live: the screen is cleared and redrawn cleanly, and shrinking
    the terminal below the minimum pauses the round behind a compact
    "resize me" overlay (showing the required and current size) until the
    terminal grows back. The gravity and play-time clocks are restarted
    after a resize, so the interruption counts as neither fall time nor
    play time. Menus and info screens repaint on resize as well.

 -- roemer2201 <r.oliver@web.de>  Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200

rowhammer (0.18.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a lock delay: a piece that lands is no longer locked immediately
    but rests for a short grace window (LOCK_DELAY_MS, 250 ms), during
    which it can still be moved left/right or rotated. The touchdown timer
    is only reset when a move makes the piece airborne again; a move that
    leaves it resting keeps the original deadline, so a piece cannot be
    stalled forever on the floor. Hard drop still locks instantly, and the
    delay does not run while paused or in the pause menu.

 -- roemer2201 <r.oliver@web.de>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0200

rowhammer (0.17.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a per-round play-time counter: the HUD shows the running round's
    elapsed time (MM:SS, paused and pause-menu time excluded) and each
    highscore entry now stores and displays that play time. The highscore
    line format gains a trailing "time" field (seconds).

 -- roemer2201 <r.oliver@web.de>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200

